 "description": "Boss DS-1 Distortion (1978), the post-1994 DS-1A circuit as ElectroSmash's analysis draws it: an input buffer, a transistor booster, an op-amp buffer and a gain stage set by Distortion, two 1N4148s clipping to VB, a Big Muff-style Tone, Level and an output buffer. Boss's JFET bypass switching isn't drawn. The 2SC2240s and the NJM3404A are our own cards from Toshiba's and Nisshinbo's sheets.",
 "tags": [
  "distortion"
 ],
